"- \"Backed by a legacy dating to 1997, Cineline India, through its flagship brand MovieMAX, is building a fast-growing, technology-led cinemas across India, blending premium experiences with accessible entertainment.\"\n- The deck frames the story as \"Emerging from a Regional Player to a National Cinema Exhibitor\", with a Screen Count Trend slide showing 21 (Apr-22), a Current count of 85, and an Estimated count FY27 of 105-110, tagged \"~4x\".\n- Deck claims \"Cineline emerged as the leading movie exhibitor in Q1 FY27, recording the highest growth in admissions, Gross Box Office Collections (GBOC), and combined GBOC + F&B revenues.\"\n- The MovieMAX Edge is stated as curated luxury design and premium F&B, \"Advanced 2K & 4K projections paired with immersive 7.1 surround sound\", and identifying high-potential hubs (a separate timeline slide cites 4K projection and Dolby Atmos from 2022).","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [Fire loss] A P&L footnote records an exceptional item being \"a WDV of Fixed assets lost in Fire at Ghaziabad and as required under IND-AS 16. Company has filed a claim with Insurance company and expected to settle in due course of time.\"\n- [Leadership] Mr. Rajeev Sharma has been appointed Joint CEO of Cineline India Limited; he was previously CEO of NY Cinemas (the multiplex chain promoted by Ajay Devgn), later Group CEO at ADF, and spent ~15 years with Fujifilm through PID Pvt. Ltd. as CEO.\n- [Promoter group] Promoters are the Kanakia family — Mr. Rasesh B. Kanakia (Chairman, started real estate development in 1986), Mr. Himanshu B. Kanakia (Managing Director) and Mr. Ashish R. Kanakia (Chief Executive Officer).\n- [Industry backdrop, Ormax Jan-Jun 2026] Jan-Jun 2026 India box office reached Rs 6,398 Cr, the highest first-half total since the pandemic, exceeding 2025 by nearly Rs 650 Cr; footfalls rose 5% YoY to 37.8 crore, reversing three years of decline.\n- [Industry concentration] Rs 100 Cr grossers fell from 17 to 13 and the top 15 films accounted for 58% of revenues (up from 49% in 2025), with Dhurandhar: The Revenge alone contributing 20% of H1 2026 collections — the deck calls this \"growing box office concentration among a few blockbuster releases\".","src":"deck","title":"Notable from the deck"}]},"sources":["investor presentation 27-07-2026","structured quarterly financials"],"thesis":"Cineline India positions itself as a legacy-backed (since 1997) cinema exhibitor scaling its MovieMAX brand from a regional player into a national, technology-led premium multiplex chain, run across four asset models with a lease-secured screen pipeline weighted toward Southern India.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[],"open_total":0,"quarters_n":0,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":3.09,"fy":"FY22","mcap":301,"opm":30.1,"pe":null,"roe":-31.1},{"de":2.04,"fy":"FY23","mcap":292,"opm":19.8,"pe":162.2,"roe":-19.4},{"de":1.53,"fy":"FY24","mcap":418,"opm":24.8,"pe":null,"roe":-1.7},{"de":0.0,"fy":"FY25","mcap":279,"opm":20.0,"pe":null,"roe":-12.2},{"de":0.78,"fy":"FY26","mcap":295,"opm":20.9,"pe":25.7,"roe":8.0}],"wtt":null},"meta":{"co":"CINELINE INDIA LIMITED","isin":"INE704H01022","s":"CINELINE","sector":"Media, Entertainment & Publication"},"s":"CINELINE"}